{
 "name": "campaign_lowvram_offload",
 "description": "Low-VRAM model offload, Sept 24 (PRs 11764 keep-CPU, 11766 pin): stock accelerate model offload copies every weight D2H into fresh pageable memory at ~1 GiB/s on each offload, keep-CPU keeps the host copy and skips that copy, pin page-locks it so H2D runs at ~52 instead of ~6.6 GiB/s. Arms per model: fast (resident, memory_mode fast), stock (memory_mode low_vram, KEEP_CPU=0 PIN=0), keep (KEEP_CPU=1 PIN=0), pin (KEEP_CPU=1 PIN=1). Needs a Studio tree containing both PRs (e.g. --set options.studio_src=pr/11766); on an older tree the env vars are ignored and keep/pin silently equal stock, so check the cell logs for the keep/pin lines (TODO(verify) the exact log text) and status.offload_policy (must be model offload, not group). Peak VRAM must not move between stock/keep/pin; host RAM does (RssAnon falls, RssFile rises with keep). One arm per process is mandatory: ru_maxrss / VmHWM are lifetime peaks. The probe's group_te arms were a monkeypatched planner and are not reproducible through Studio options; they were rejected (1.3-1.6x host RAM). Video cells pass guidance and fps as null so Studio's family defaults apply, as the original probe did (it passed neither).",
